WEBVTT

00:08:28.118 --> 00:08:30.786
AG: I am absolutely
using this as an excuse.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:33.196
It's not me, it's not
that I lack willpower.

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:35.756
This is just a very procrastinogenic task.

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:39.316
FS: Yeah, tasks
that don't give you autonomy,

00:08:39.340 --> 00:08:41.096
that lack structure,

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.666
and that are ambiguous.

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:45.989
AG: Is that why so many writers
struggle with procrastination?

00:08:46.013 --> 00:08:47.183
FS: It could be.

00:08:47.207 --> 00:08:48.865
Because yeah, when you're writing,

00:08:48.889 --> 00:08:50.805
who's telling you what the next thing is

00:08:50.829 --> 00:08:52.972
you're supposed to be
writing, right? You are.

00:08:52.996 --> 00:08:55.332
I mean, it brings up uncertainty
about yourself.

00:08:55.356 --> 00:08:58.650
It brings up doubts about whether
you know what you're doing, right?

00:08:58.674 --> 00:09:00.816
We all have that feeling
from time to time.